     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is twice that. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release metformin.\n- **1,700 mg per day,** for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** Please tell me the intended dose and frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. A pharmacist review would also be a good idea."
      }
